    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (83.08) serving as our undisputed anchor. His matchup against Rocker is the quintessential \"green light\" scenario; between the favorable SP skill and a slow opposing delivery that heavily inflates his stolen base probability, he is the engine of our offensive ceiling. Following closely, **Mickey Moniak** (71.83) offers an elite platoon edge, with the model identifying a 14% boost against the right-handed Keller, making him a high-efficiency play despite a slight park penalty. **James Wood** (67.92) also warrants attention at the top of the order; his elite xwOBA metrics combined with the stability of the leadoff spot solidify him as a core component of our expected run production today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros** (47.34), who flirted with the 50-point mark but ultimately fell short due to a neutral platoon profile and the defensive efficiency of the opposing backstop. While **Kyle Karros** projected slightly better than **Cole Young** in terms of pure base skill, the volatility of the latter\u2019s stolen base upside against McCullers Jr. forced our hand. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Vinnie Pasquantino** (57.00); while his raw power is notable, his 15% penalty due to the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Schultz keeps him tethered to the fringe of our starting requirements. We will continue monitoring the status of **Tyler Soderstrom**, who remains on our radar for potential future deployment, but with our current configuration, we are effectively optimized to maximize sprint-speed opportunities against today's targetable pitching staff.",
